an overseas trip by house speaker nancy  pelosi is causing big friction with  china this morning she has just left  taiwan's capital after visiting the  national legislature and meeting with  the country's president the move has  upset china which considers taiwan to be  a rogue province it is responding with  military exercises around the island  nation our adam yamaguchi is there  good morning speaker nancy pelosi just  wrapped up a whirlwind but potentially  consequential visit to taiwan in the  face of threats from china she struck a  defiant tone and emphasized that america  would not abandon its commitment to  taiwan  america's determination to preserve  democracy here in taiwan and around the  world  remains ironclad  meeting with taiwanese president saint  nguyen  pelosi became the most senior u.s  official to visit taiwan in 25 years  the chinese foreign ministry called her  trip a complete farce warning that those  who offend china will be punished  shortly after the speaker landed china  announced plans for live fire military  drills and water surrounding taiwan a  move the taiwanese said demonstrates an  intention to destroy regional peace  what matters to us  is that we salute the successes of  taiwan  we work together for the security of  taiwan  china claims the island as its territory  and opposes any engagement by taiwanese  officials with foreign governments  pelosi's last stop in taiwan was the  museum of human rights  this is significant because human rights  is something that is near and dear to  her heart she first sort of made a big  name for herself in tiananmen square in  in china many many years ago this is  clearly a message  but on the streets of taipei some locals  expressed concern about how the visit  will impact them  these two great countries fighting for  power he says taiwan is stuck in the  middle taiwan is a small country we have  to try to survive  what happens tomorrow and beyond is the  question many here are now asking  will 